  "prediction": "They evaluate their resulting word embeddings through IV and OOV evaluations, observing improvements on rare word representation, syntactic tasks, and statistically significant gains on the chunking task. However, they note that downstream task performance may not significantly improve due to OOV words being mapped to the \"$\\langle$ unk $\\rangle$\" token. They also plan to investigate the trade-off between semantics and syntax and the potential for tunable representations in future work.",
  "scored_prediction": "They evaluate their resulting word embeddings through IV and OOV evaluations, observing improvements on rare word representation, syntactic tasks, and statistically significant gains on the chunking task. However, they note that downstream task performance may not significantly improve due to OOV words being mapped to the \"$\\langle$ unk $\\rangle$\" token. They also plan to investigate the trade-off between semantics and syntax and the potential for tunable representations in future work.",
  "score": 22.90076335877863,
  "answers": [
    "We also evaluate all five models on downstream tasks from the VecEval suite BIBREF13 , using only the tasks for which training and evaluation data is freely available: chunking, sentiment and question classification, and natural language identification (NLI). The default settings from the suite are used, but we run only the fixed settings, where the embeddings themselves are not tunable parameters of the models, forcing the system to use only the information already in the embeddings."
  ],
